      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my 2018 civic is making this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a worn one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt on your 2018 Civic is responsible for driving multiple peripheral components like the alternator, power steering pump, water pump, air conditioning compressor, and sometimes the radiator fan. A worn serpentine belt can deteriorate, leading to reduced flexibility and grip. Reinforcement inside the belt can cause it to slip on the pulleys, resulting in a squealing noise when you step on the gas and engage heavier engine loads. It's best to inspect the belt and consider an adjustment or replacement if necessary.",
